  "body": "The release heavy lane plans one step for each test binary of motion and app. Kernel has no such split. Plan one `kernel heavy` step for each kernel test binary that holds an `#[ignore]`d test.\n\nAdding kernel heavy steps is a coverage change. The release tier runs kernel `--ignored` tests for the first time.\n\nFound in the review of PR #1737.\n\nPart of #1714.\n\nDone means: `cargo xtask gate release --dry-run` lists one kernel heavy step for each kernel test binary with an `#[ignore]`d test, and a unit test pins that each such binary has a step.\n",
